<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17278" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex-sūcus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exūcus</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exsuccus</span></b> ), 
		a, um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>without juice</i>, <i>sapless</i> (postAug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corporis substantia exsucior,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Anim. 51</span></i>
			: juvenis membris exsucior, Auct. Itin. Alex.
			6.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(oratores) aridi et exsuci et exsangues,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 12, 10, 15</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
